choice":"nose up bank left"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51ba","isCorrect":false,"choice":"nose up wings level"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51bb","isCorrect":false,"choice":"bank and pitch correct"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ed9","question":"The needle and ball of a Turn Indicator are both to the left of the datum. This indicates:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51bc","isCorrect":true,"choice":"a left turn with too much bank"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51bd","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a left turn with too little bank"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51be","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a right turn with too little bank"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51bf","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a right turn with too much bank"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eda","question":"Under conditions determined by the International Standard Atmosphere, at MSL True Air Speed is:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"greater than CAS"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"less than CAS"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"equals CAS"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"is indeterminate due to the variation in temperature"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7edb","question":"In what range is GPWS operative?","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"2450 - 0 ft"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c5","isCorrect":false,"choice":"3000 - 50 ft"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c6","isCorrect":true,"choice":"2450 - 50 ft"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51c7","isCorrect":