"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7edf","question":"What is used for EGT measurement?","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51d4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"helical bi-metallic strips"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51d5","isCorrect":false,"choice":"thermistors"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51d6","isCorrect":false,"choice":"radiation pyrometry"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51d7","isCorrect":true,"choice":"thermo emf thermocouples"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee0","question":"When accelerating on a northerly heading what does the Direct Reading Magnetic Compass indicate?","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51d8","isCorrect":false,"choice":"no change"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51d9","isCorrect":true,"choice":"north"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51da","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a turn to the west"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51db","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a turn to the east"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee1","question":"Why is there a vibration device in a pressure altimeter? i to prevent hysteresis ii to prevent lag in a mechanical system iii to keep pilots happy during long flights iv to prevent icing v to overcome dither","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51dc","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii iv"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51dd","isCorrect":true,"choice":"i ii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51de","isCorrect":false,"choice":"ii iii v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51df","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii iii"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee2","question":"What does the white arc on a temperature scale indicate?","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"never exceed"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"maximum start and acceleration temperature"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"normal operating temperature"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"minimum temperature"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee3","question":"The rate of turn indicator is a very useful gyroscopic instrument. When used in conjunction with the Attitude Indicator it provides:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e4","isCorrect":false,"choice":"angle of bank"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e5","isCorrect":true,"choice":"rate of turn about the yaw axis"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e6","isCorrect":false,"choice":"rate of climb"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e7","isCorrect":false,"choice":"rate of turn athwartships"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee4","question":"With the aircraft weight constant but variations in airfield altitude, take-off will always be at a constant:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e8","isCorrect":false,"choice":"equivalent airspeed"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51e9","isCorrect":true,"choice":"calibrated airspeed"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51ea","isCorrect":false,"choice":"groundspeed"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51eb","isCorrect":false,"choice":"true air speed"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee5","question":"An inertial reference system is aligned when turned on so as to:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51ec","isCorrect":true,"choice":"calculate the computed trihedron with reference to the earth"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51ed","isCorrect":false,"choice":"establish true and magnetic north"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51ee","isCorrect":false,"choice":"establish position relative to true and magnetic north"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51ef","isCorrect":false,"choice":"establish magnetic north"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee6","question":"Total Air Temperature is __________ than static air temperature and the difference varies with __________","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f0","isCorrect":false,"choice":"warmer altitude"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f1","isCorrect":false,"choice":"colder altitude"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f2","isCorrect":true,"choice":"warmer CAS"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f3","isCorrect":false,"choice":"colder CAS"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee7","question":"True heading can be converted into magnetic heading using a compass and:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f4","isCorrect":true,"choice":"a map with isogonal lines"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f5","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a map with isoclinal lines"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f6","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a map with isobars"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f7","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a deviation card"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee8","question":"An aircraft flies into a colder airmass. This will cause the altimeter to:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f8","isCorrect":true,"choice":"over-read"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51f9","isCorrect":false,"choice":"under-read"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51fa","isCorrect":false,"choice":"read the correct altitude"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51fb","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the indication will depend on the hemisphere of operation"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ee9","question":"A gravity-erecting device is utilised in:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51fc","isCorrect":true,"choice":"an artificial horizon"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51fd","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a directional gyroscopic indicator"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51fe","isCorrect":false,"choice":"vertical speed indicator"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c51ff","isCorrect":false,"choice":"aturn and slip"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eea","question":"The rigidity of a gyroscope can be improved by:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5200","isCorrect":true,"choice":"increasing the angular momentum and concentrating the mass on the periphery of the rotor"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5201","isCorrect":false,"choice":"increasing the angular momentum and concentrating the mass at the hub of the rotor"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5202","isCorrect":false,"choice":"decreasing the angular momentum and concentrating the mass on the periphery of the rotor"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5203","isCorrect":false,"choice":"decreasing the angular momentum and concentrating the mass at the hub of the rotor"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eeb","question":"The outputs of a flux valve are initially sent to:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5204","isCorrect":false,"choice":"an amplifier"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5205","isCorrect":true,"choice":"an error detector"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5206","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a compass card"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5207","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a feedback loop"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eec","question":"The period of validity of an FMS data base is:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5208","isCorrect":false,"choice":"56 days"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5209","isCorrect":false,"choice":"one week"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c520a","isCorrect":true,"choice":"28 days"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c520b","isCorrect":false,"choice":"varies depending on the area of operational cover"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eed","question":"An IRS differs from an INS in that it:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c520c","isCorrect":false,"choice":"has a longer spin-up (is not affected by vertical accelerations due to gravity)"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c520d","isCorrect":true,"choice":"has a shorter spin-up time and suffers from laser lock."},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c520e","isCorrect":false,"choice":"does not need to correct for coriolis and central acceleration)"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c520f","isCorrect":false,"choice":"does not experience Schuler errors as accelerometers are strapped down and not rotated by a feedback loop"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eee","question":"In a solid state gyroscope the purpose of the dither motor is to:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5210","isCorrect":false,"choice":"enhance the acceleration of the gyro at all rotational rates"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5211","isCorrect":true,"choice":"overcome laser lock"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5212","isCorrect":false,"choice":"compensate for transport wander"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5213","isCorrect":false,"choice":"stabilise the laser frequencies"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eef","question":"In an IRS:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5214","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the accelerometers are strapped down but the platform is gyro-stabilised"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5215","isCorrect":false,"choice":"the platform is strapped down but the accelerometers are gyro-stabilised"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5216","isCorrect":false,"choice":"accelerometers and gyros are both gyro-stabilised"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5217","isCorrect":true,"choice":"accelerometers and gyros are both strapped down"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ef0","question":"Which of the following correctly describes the gyroscope of a Rate of Turn Indicator? i 1 degree of freedom ii 2 degrees of freedom iii its frame is held by two springs iv its spin axis is parallel to the pitch axis v the spin axis is parallel to the yaw axis vi the spin axis is horizontal","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5218","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5219","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i iv v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c521a","isCorrect":true,"choice":"i iii v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c521b","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i iii vi"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ef1","question":"A blockage occurs in the ram air source and the drain-hole. The ASI in a non-pressurised aircraft will:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c521c","isCorrect":false,"choice":"read a little low"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c521d","isCorrect":false,"choice":"read a little high"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c521e","isCorrect":true,"choice":"act like an altimeter"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c521f","isCorrect":false,"choice":"freeze at zero"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ef2","question":"The errors associated with the Directional Indicator are: i earth rate ii transport wander iii banking when pitched up iv annual movement of the poles v mechanical problems","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5220","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii iii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5221","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii iv v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5222","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii iii iv v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5223","isCorrect":true,"choice":"i ii iii v"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ef3","question":"A rate integrating gyroscope is used in: i inertial attitude system ii automatic flight control systems iii inertial navigation systems iv rate of turn indicators","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5224","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5225","isCorrect":true,"choice":"i iii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5226","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i iii iv"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5227","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii iii"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7ef4","question":"Rate of turn is affected by: i aircraft speed ii angle of bank iii aircraft weight","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5228","isCorrect":true,"choice":"i ii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5229","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i iii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c522a","isCorrect":fa