lotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7efe","question":"The angle formed between the directive force and the total magnetic force is called:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5250","isCorrect":false,"choice":"variation"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5251","isCorrect":false,"choice":"deviation"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5252","isCorrect":true,"choice":"dip"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5253","isCorrect":false,"choice":"isoclinal"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7eff","question":"What is the speed of sound at 30,000 ft and -40°C?","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5254","isCorrect":false,"choice":"562 kt"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5255","isCorrect":true,"choice":"595 kt"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5256","isCorrect":false,"choice":"590 kt"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5257","isCorrect":false,"choice":"661 kt"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f00","question":"If a constant CAS is maintained under normal conditions in the climb what happens to the Mach No?","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5258","isCorrect":false,"choice":"it will decrease"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5259","isCorrect":false,"choice":"it will remain constant"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c525a","isCorrect":false,"choice":"it will decrease in an isothermal layer"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c525b","isCorrect":true,"choice":"it will increase"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f01","question":"Regarding magnetism; which of the following statements is correct? i lines of flux run from blue pole to red pole ii like poles repel iii unlike poles repel iv like poles attract v unlike poles attract","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c525c","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c525d","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i iii v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c525e","isCorrect":true,"choice":"ii v"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c525f","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i iii iv"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f02","question":"The output of a double integration N/S is:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5260","isCorrect":false,"choice":"velocity"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5261","isCorrect":false,"choice":"departure"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5262","isCorrect":true,"choice":"distance"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5263","isCorrect":false,"choice":"longitude"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f03","question":"A solid state gyro is:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5264","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a rate gyro"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5265","isCorrect":true,"choice":"a rate sensor"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5266","isCorrect":false,"choice":"an earth gyro"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5267","isCorrect":false,"choice":"a tied gyro"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f04","question":"The magnetic heading reference unit has a precession rate of:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5268","isCorrect":false,"choice":"1°/min"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5269","isCorrect":true,"choice":"2°/min"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c526a","isCorrect":false,"choice":"5°/min"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c526b","isCorrect":false,"choice":"3°/min"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f05","question":"If the TAS at 40,000 ft is 450 kt the Mach No is:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c526c","isCorrect":false,"choice":"0·815"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c526d","isCorrect":true,"choice":"0·783"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c526e","isCorrect":false,"choice":"0·76"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c526f","isCorrect":false,"choice":"0·825"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f06","question":"The EADI and the EHSI of an EFIS installation are also referred to by the manufacturers as:","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5270","isCorrect":true,"choice":"primary display and navigation display respectively"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5271","isCorrect":false,"choice":"navigation display and primary display respectively"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5272","isCorrect":false,"choice":"EICAS and ECAM respectively"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5273","isCorrect":false,"choice":"ECAM and EICAS respectively"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7f07","question":"In which of the following modes may information from the AWR be displayed? ii expanded ILS iii map iv full nav v full ILS vi expanded nav vii full VOR viii expanded VOR ix centre map","choices":[{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5274","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i ii iv vii"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5275","isCorrect":false,"choice":"i iii vii viii ix"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5276","isCorrect":true,"choice":"ii iii vi viii ix"},{"_id":"693a8ce8cba8ac949a6c5277","isCorrect":false,"choice":"ii iii v vii ix"}],"explanation":null,"subject":"Instruments","book":"Pilotshala Practice Set","topic":"Revision 3"},{"image":"","difficulty":"medium","_id":"683fe728452555c3884c7